<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Java</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jawa Barat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a> is a province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a> in the western part of the island of Java, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandung">Bandung</a>. It is the most populous province of the country and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the Sundanese people, and it covers much of the territory of the old Sunda Kingdom. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banten">Banten</a>, formerly part of the province, became a separate province in 2000.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-java.jpg" alt="West Java" width="320" height="147" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: TUBS · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:West_Java_in_Indonesia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
